        "original_id": "4e722f16-73e2-5733-ae7a-47f991970d07",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-François Clervoy, Thomas Reiter\n- Organizations: CNES, ESA, NASA, German Air Force\n- Missions: NASA Space Shuttle missions, STS-121, Expedition 14\n- Places: Frankfurt, West Germany, ISS\n- Roles: astronaut, engineer, Brigadier General, ESA Interagency Coordinator, Advisor to the Director General\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Reiter was born on 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany.\n- Jean-François André Clervoy was born on 19 November 1958.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Thomas Reiter is a retired European astronaut and a Brigadier General in the German Air Force.\n- Thomas Reiter currently works as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at the European Space Agency.\n- Thomas Reiter arrived at the ISS on 6 July 2006 aboard Space Shuttle Discovery during mission STS-121.\n- During Expedition 14, Thomas Reiter had already joined the ISS crew after arriving on STS-121.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
